WHAT WAS BUILT
--------------
The web HelixPage is a thin shell: it reads `useSettings()` only for its
`isLoading` flag and hands that to `<PageContainer loading=…>`, which renders a
centered spinner while loading and otherwise renders its child `<AISettings/>`.
The native parity reproduces that composition verbatim, SwiftUI-native (no web
clone), adaptive macOS + iOS:

  apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Settings/
    HelixPage.swift              — HelixPage<Content> View: breadcrumb + header +
                                   settings-gated body; success body = embedded
                                   AISettings (web <PageContainer><AISettings/>).
    HelixPage.Projection.swift   — HelixSettingsInput + HelixPagePhase +
                                   HelixPageProjection (pure web PageContainer
                                   body gate: loading/empty/error/success).
    HelixPage.Model.swift        — @Observable HelixPageModel (binds useSettings
                                   via HelixSettingsSource seam, P1/S8), P1/S11
                                   view.opened telemetry, InMemoryHelixSettingsSource,
                                   HelixPageStrings i18n facade (P1/S10).
    HelixPage.Views.swift        — HelixBreadcrumb, HelixPageHeader,
                                   HelixPageLoadingView / EmptyView / ErrorView.
    HelixPage.Previews.swift     — #Preview per state (success off/cloud, loading,
                                   empty, error) in a NavigationStack.
    HelixPage.Tests.swift        — XCTest: projection + model + strings + nav.
    HelixRouteRegistration.swift — HelixRoute value, /integrations/helix deep-link
                                   resolver, helixNavigationDestination() modifier,
                                   page() factory composing HelixPage<AISettings>.

  Navigation registration (allowed):
    Sources/Platform/Settings/SettingsScene.swift — settings route host now applies
      .helixNavigationDestination() so HelixPage is a real NavigationStack
      destination (shell NavigationSplitView/Stack), reachable by pushing HelixRoute.
    project.yml + .swiftlint.yml — TeslaSync/Features added to app-target sources +
      lint scope so the page compiles and is linted.

  Strings (platform catalog):
    Localization/Localizable.xcstrings — 8 keys added (3 web-parity + 5 chrome).

ADAPTIVE / HIG / a11y / units
  • Adaptive: ScrollView + token spacing; #if os(iOS) inline nav title; macOS regular.
  • Tokens only (P2 Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius); materials via
    TSGlassPanel (AISettings child). No hardcoded colors/typography.
  • a11y: TSPageTitle .isHeader; breadcrumb crumbs individually voiced; loading
    body labeled; error body combined; ≥44pt TSButton targets; Dynamic Type +
    light/dark + increased-contrast inherited from the token layer (ADR-015).
  • Live data: settings is a GET (not an SSE source) → no live/staleness axis on
    the page (the AISettings child owns its own freshness chip). Per manifest the
    declared states are loading + success.
  • Units: no SI quantities rendered by the page chrome (display-boundary rule N/A).

